From 77e1db2cbac4e0027523e5e6ffbd0dc2c463fcea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:25:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER (tools 0149): one stop stops everything; Ctrl+F
 only shows the designer's find box
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 1003: "紅色停止鍵好像有兩個地方會出現 我想要按任何一個 都要完全停止"
- The status bar's and the Solution Explorer toolbar's stop button both run
  ht9045Designer.run.stopAll: cancel our build, stop every debug session
  (vscode.debug.stopDebugging()), then taskkill /T /F any wb_serve / wb_publish /
  wb_gateway exe of this tree still alive (other folders untouched).
- Stop is lit when a wb_* exe runs with no session (tasklist every 3 s).
- VS Code's own stop (floating debug bar / Shift+F5) ending one of this tree's
  sessions also stops the tree's other sessions (F5's wb_publish + wb_gateway pair).

EastSun 1003: "我ctrl+F 還是會出現預設的視窗 讓我以為在他那邊搜尋"
- Ctrl+F on the designer page also opens the designer's find box; opening it
  closes VS Code's find widget left over from before.

Also: cppbridge.serverHook leaves form.event's own after-ack call
(W906_FormEventRunAfterAck, added to wb_serve.cpp 1003) out of the htd.event
copy; any other unknown FormEvent call = refused, not guessed.

Tests: run_all 3/3 layers (lib 182, extension 224); real VS Code 156/159
(the 3 known stale checks; BtnPanelLane3 / Alias came and went once this
afternoon -- the failure detail now says what the test saw).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
